From 2d04cb44bb267f4531ef20487dd77d5c085c2515 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nathan Singh <nathan.singh@hotmail.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 08:53:04 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] Arena: more Reloaded engine rules (guard, heal, revive,
 effect ids, stages, recovery, caps, summons by turn)

The next engine rules of the Golden Sun Reloaded rebalance (forum.goldensunhacking.net
topic 2779), read from its patch against an unmodified build and written again in C,
each behind its own ARENA_RULES_* switch (on by default, stock code kept for 0):
- GUARD: Total Defense takes a third of the damage, not a tenth.
- HEAL: the healer's element power counts half as much; Ember restores a tenth of max PP.
- REVIVE: a revival restores max HP x power / 1000 + 1 (at most max), from the ability's
  power; a power of 0 keeps the stock amount. Battle and the item menu.
- EFFECT_IDS: effect ids 8, 12, 16, 21, 22, 30, 36 to 41, 43 and 54 run another effect's
  handler, so the data can give one handler several odds (needs the ability data).
- DURATIONS: Impact, Guard and Ward last 5 turns, Luff is a Bind, the curse counts 4.
- STAGES: a Defense stage is 3/16 of the stat, a Resistance stage 15 (calculation, the
  messages and the status screen).
- RECOVERY: the early-recovery roll counts luck once and level / 2 against it; new base
  chances for Attack, Defense, Resistance, stun, sleep and Bind.
- STATUS: haunt takes its share 103 times in 256, a deluded attack misses 70 percent
  and a deluded unit never unleashes.
- CLASS20: class multipliers are in twentieths (needs the class data doubled).
- CAPS: element power and resistance and PP regeneration reach 255.
- ITEMS: stat-boost items give exactly their power.
- SUMMON_TURNS: the 3-Djinn summons wait for turn 2 and the 4-Djinn ones for turn 3
  (BattleWork.arenaTurn).
- AILMENTS also gains the Ailment attribute: Unit_Calculate sums equipment effect 24
  into Unit.unused[0].

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
